[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) was merged by subject line ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject))
and marked known with one fix queued. Read by tenant, form and body, it holds three problems.
Each needs its own fix and has its own ticket.

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} {tickets} />

<Callout kind="warn">
The parser fix alone does not close #4471. <code>hint</code> and <code>one-day</code> reports keep coming after it ships.
</Callout>

## The three problems

- **`parser`**: the shared parser reads dates month first, and day-first tenants write the day first. Day and month swap.
- **`hint`**: booking-v3's form prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field, then reads the date the tenant's way.
  People type what the hint says. Day and month swap again, but the fix is in the form. These are reports
  through the `form` channel from day-first tenants on booking-v3.
- **`one-day`**: the date moves one day earlier with no swap, e.g. Tuesday 12 May shown as Monday 11 May.
  The desk already read these as one-day moves (`desk-notes.json`). The cause is not verified. It looks like a time-zone
  conversion of a date-only booking. Engineering has to check it in sched-prod.

## How this was counted

- One report per id. The export pages overlap, so some reports appear twice.
- Placed by tenant locale, form and channel (`causes.ts`), not by the intake tag. The intake tag guesses from the
  reporter's browser and disagrees with the tenant often.
- One-day moves come from the desk's notes and count only under `one-day`.

